## utils.ts

Improved error handling to explicitly log the fix instructions to the browser console when recursion is detected.

The "Infinite recursion" error confirms that the database policies for `subjects` and `subject_enrollments` are checking each other in a loop (e.g., "Can I view this subject? Check if I'm enrolled." -> "Can I view this enrollment? Check if I'm the teacher of the subject." -> "Can I view this subject?").

To fix this, you must run a SQL script that replaces these circular policies with optimized versions using `SECURITY DEFINER` functions (which bypass RLS to break the loop) and simplifies the `subjects` view policy.

I have updated the **Enroll Subject Modal** and **Confirmation Modal** to explicitly provide this SQL script in the UI when this error occurs, allowing you to easily copy and run it in your Supabase dashboard.

